  "verbalization": "The compound [(1'R,2S,2'R,3'R,5'S,8'R,9'R,10'R,13'S)-2',9',13'-triacetyloxy-10'-hydroxy-8',12',15',15'-tetramethylspiro[oxirane-2,4'-tricyclo[9.3.1.03,8]pentadec-11-ene]-5'-yl] (3R)-3-(dimethylamino)-3-phenylpropanoate) is consistently identified as a target of the Kappa-type opioid receptor across three distinct paths, with a final score of 0.7512. This compound is known to interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which in turn is targeted by multiple drugs, including 3-Methylfentanyl and Ginkgolide A, both of which are linked to the Kappa-type opioid receptor. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism involving the activation of the Kappa-type opioid receptor through interactions with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, possibly through shared signaling pathways or receptor cross-talk. The consistent targeting of the Kappa-type opioid receptor by this compound, across different drugs and analytical standards, supports a plausible role in opioid receptor modulation. The evidence is robust and suggests a clear, biologically plausible relationship between the compound and the Kappa-type opioid receptor."
